publican national position, would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Tom Barrett (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 7th District sits right at partisan even, but Republican incumbent Tom Barrett is defending it in a strongly favorable Democratic national environment. Ten expert ratings split between tossup and Democratic favor, with none backing Barrett, and prediction markets price William Lawrence around the mid-70s percent to win. The only recent independent poll, from Emerson College in mid-October, showed Lawrence ahead 53-45, though earlier Democratic-sponsored surveys had the race much closer.\n\nMoney has poured in from both sides. Barrett has raised more than twice Lawrence's total, but outside groups have spent heavily against him in what reports call the nation's most expensive House advertising race, and Lawrence's cash on hand is essentially even. That combination of environment, polling, and outside spending gives Lawrence the edge, while Barrett's incumbency and the district's even lean keep the outcome genuinely in doubt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7073, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7167, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7145, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7121, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6654, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6515, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6531, "marg